                                    <h1>Shopify vs WooCommerce for D2C India 2026 &mdash; Real Cost, Customisation &amp; Which Wins by Stage</h1>

                                    <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> Both work for D2C in India in 2026. <strong>Shopify wins for speed-to-launch + reliability + native ecosystem</strong> (especially at &#8377;1Cr&ndash;&#8377;30Cr ARR). <strong>WooCommerce wins for total cost of ownership at scale + customisation depth + brand control</strong> (especially at &gt;&#8377;30Cr ARR or content-heavy brands). The deciding factor is rarely &lsquo;features&rsquo; &mdash; it&rsquo;s where you want to spend engineering time: on the platform (Shopify constraints + apps), or on infrastructure (WooCommerce hosting + custom code). Below: real TCO math, when each wins, and red flags to watch.</p>
                                    <p>This is the honest comparison we give D2C founders deciding between Shopify and WooCommerce in 2026. Real total cost of ownership at each ARR stage, customisation depth, performance + scaling limits, and the 3 cases when each absolutely wins. From inside the ecommerce build agency model.</p>

                                    <h2>TL;DR &mdash; The Comparison at a Glance (2026)</h2>
                                    <table class="cmp-table"><thead><tr><th>Criteria</th><th>Shopify</th><th>WooCommerce</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Best for</strong></td><td>Speed-to-launch, &#8377;1Cr&ndash;&#8377;30Cr ARR D2C</td><td>Brand control + customisation + &gt;&#8377;30Cr ARR or content-heavy</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Subscription fee</strong></td><td>$29&ndash;$2,000+/mo (Basic to Plus)</td><td>Free core, hosting &#8377;1K&ndash;&#8377;30K/mo</td></tr><tr><td><strong>App / plugin costs</strong></td><td>$200&ndash;$2,000+/mo at scale</td><td>Many free; premium &#8377;5K&ndash;&#8377;40K/yr</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Transaction fees</strong></td><td>0.5&ndash;2% if not using Shopify Payments</td><td>None (gateway only)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Speed-to-launch</strong></td><td><strong>1&ndash;3 weeks</strong></td><td>3&ndash;8 weeks</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Performance / Core Web Vitals</strong></td><td>Good (with optimised theme)</td><td><strong>Excellent if engineered right</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Customisation depth</strong></td><td>Limited by Shopify architecture</td><td><strong>Unlimited (open source)</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>SEO control</strong></td><td>Good (some constraints)</td><td><strong>Full control</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Scaling limit</strong></td><td>Shopify Plus handles &#8377;500Cr+ GMV</td><td>Scales with infrastructure investment</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Maintenance burden</strong></td><td><strong>Low (Shopify hosts)</strong></td><td>Higher (you host)</td></tr></tbody></table>

                                    <h2>Real Total Cost of Ownership (Honest D2C Numbers)</h2>
<h3>Year 1 TCO at &#8377;3Cr ARR D2C</h3><table class='cmp-table'><thead><tr><th>Cost component</th><th>Shopify</th><th>WooCommerce</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Platform / hosting</td><td>$79/mo &times; 12 = ~&#8377;75K/yr</td><td>&#8377;3K/mo hosting &times; 12 = ~&#8377;36K/yr</td></tr><tr><td>Apps / plugins</td><td>$400/mo &times; 12 = ~&#8377;3.8L/yr</td><td>&#8377;5K/mo &times; 12 = ~&#8377;60K/yr</td></tr><tr><td>Initial build</td><td>~&#8377;3L (theme + setup)</td><td>~&#8377;6L (full custom build)</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance / dev</td><td>~&#8377;1.5L/yr</td><td>~&#8377;3L/yr (hosting + plugin mgmt)</td></tr><tr><td>Transaction fees (if non-Shopify Payments)</td><td>2% of &#8377;3Cr = &#8377;6L/yr</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total Year 1</strong></td><td><strong>~&#8377;14.5L</strong> (with non-Shopify Payments)</td><td><strong>~&#8377;9.6L</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>Year 1 TCO at &#8377;30Cr ARR D2C (Plus tier)</h3><table class='cmp-table'><thead><tr><th>Cost component</th><th>Shopify Plus</th><th>WooCommerce (scaled hosting)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Platform / hosting</td><td>$2,000/mo &times; 12 = ~&#8377;20L/yr</td><td>&#8377;30K/mo hosting &times; 12 = ~&#8377;3.6L/yr</td></tr><tr><td>Apps / plugins</td><td>$1,500/mo = ~&#8377;15L/yr</td><td>&#8377;15K/mo = ~&#8377;1.8L/yr</td></tr><tr><td>Initial build / migration</td><td>~&#8377;15L</td><td>~&#8377;25L</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance / dev pod</td><td>~&#8377;6L/yr</td><td>~&#8377;15L/yr (engineering team)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total Year 1</strong></td><td><strong>~&#8377;56L</strong></td><td><strong>~&#8377;45L</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>
<div class='verdict'><strong>Honest take:</strong> Shopify TCO is higher at every stage. The premium buys you: speed-to-launch, lower ops burden, native ecosystem. At &lt;&#8377;30Cr ARR most brands willingly pay it. At &gt;&#8377;30Cr ARR the math flips for content-heavy or customisation-heavy brands.</div>
<h2>Where Shopify Genuinely Wins</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Speed-to-launch.</strong> Live in 1&ndash;3 weeks from theme to launch. WooCommerce takes 3&ndash;8 weeks.</li><li><strong>Native ecosystem.</strong> Klaviyo, Interakt, Shopify Inbox, Shop Pay, Recharge, ReConvert, LoyaltyLion, Smile.io &mdash; D2C tools integrate Shopify-first.</li><li><strong>Reliability.</strong> 99.99% uptime SLA. No hosting concerns, no security patches, no plugin conflicts.</li><li><strong>Low ops burden.</strong> No DevOps + no security audits + no scaling concerns. Founder + small team can run.</li><li><strong>Shop Pay + Magic Checkout for conversion.</strong> 15&ndash;25% conversion lift via accelerated checkout.</li></ul>
<h2>Where WooCommerce Genuinely Wins</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Customisation depth.</strong> Open source. Modify any line of code. Custom product types, custom workflows, custom integrations &mdash; no Shopify architecture constraint.</li><li><strong>SEO control.</strong> Full URL structure, schema, hreflang, headers control. Beats Shopify for content-heavy brands.</li><li><strong>Brand + content focus.</strong> WordPress + WooCommerce wins for brands where the content engine (blog + magazine + storytelling) is the marketing moat.</li><li><strong>Total cost at scale.</strong> Above &#8377;30Cr ARR, WooCommerce TCO is often 30&ndash;50% lower than Shopify Plus.</li><li><strong>Data ownership.</strong> Your hosting + your database + your full control. Shopify holds the customer data on their servers.</li></ul>
<h2>3 Cases Where One Absolutely Beats the Other</h2>
<h3>Shopify absolutely beats WooCommerce when&hellip;</h3><p>You&rsquo;re launching a D2C MVP in &lt;3 weeks, you&rsquo;re below &#8377;30Cr ARR, you don&rsquo;t have an engineering team, OR you want speed + reliability + lowest ops burden. Default to Shopify here.</p>
<h3>WooCommerce absolutely beats Shopify when&hellip;</h3><p>You&rsquo;re above &#8377;30Cr ARR + content-heavy (blog drives 30%+ of traffic), OR you need custom workflows Shopify can&rsquo;t support (B2B pricing, complex multi-vendor, custom product configurators), OR full data ownership matters legally / strategically.</p>
<h3>Pick neither &mdash; go headless when&hellip;</h3><p>You&rsquo;re &gt;&#8377;50Cr ARR + need Core Web Vitals dominance + brand storytelling moat + multi-market scaling. Headless commerce (Hydrogen on Shopify, Next.js + Sanity / Contentful on Wagtail/Woo backend) wins above this size. <a href='Shopify_Plus_vs_Headless_for_Scaling_D2C_Brands.php'>See our Shopify Plus vs Headless deep-dive</a>.</p>
