                                    <h2>FAQs</h2>
<h3>Is Shopify or WooCommerce cheaper for a D2C brand in India?</h3>
<p><strong>WooCommerce is cheaper on subscription + transaction fees.</strong> But Shopify is cheaper on total cost when you factor in ops + maintenance + reliability + speed-to-launch. Below &#8377;3Cr ARR, Shopify TCO is typically &#8377;3L&ndash;&#8377;6L higher; above &#8377;30Cr ARR, WooCommerce can be 30&ndash;50% lower TCO.</p>
<h3>Can WooCommerce handle &gt;&#8377;30Cr ARR D2C scale?</h3>
<p>Yes, but it requires real engineering investment &mdash; managed WordPress hosting (WP Engine, Kinsta), caching (Redis, Cloudflare), CDN, plugin discipline. Brands at &gt;&#8377;100Cr ARR (like Wow Skin Science, MyGlamm) have run on WooCommerce or migrated to headless.</p>
<h3>What about Shopify Plus vs WooCommerce at &gt;&#8377;30Cr ARR?</h3>
<p>Both work. Shopify Plus is faster to operationalise. WooCommerce gives you more control + lower long-term TCO. The decision usually comes down to engineering team capability + content + customisation needs.</p>
<h3>Is Shopify SEO worse than WooCommerce?</h3>
<p><strong>WooCommerce has more SEO control</strong> (full URL structure, custom schema, custom robots / sitemap rules). <strong>Shopify is &lsquo;good-enough&rsquo; SEO</strong> for most D2C; only matters at scale or content-heavy.</p>
<h3>Should I go headless (Hydrogen / Next.js + Sanity) instead?</h3>
<p>Go headless at &gt;&#8377;50Cr ARR or when Core Web Vitals + multi-market scale + brand storytelling moat are critical. Below that, headless is over-engineered for D2C.</p>
<h3>Can I migrate from Shopify to WooCommerce later?</h3>
<p>Yes &mdash; product data + customer data + order history all migrate. But it&rsquo;s ~&#8377;3L&ndash;&#8377;8L in engineering work + 4&ndash;8 weeks. Plan migration carefully; don&rsquo;t default-launch on something you&rsquo;ll need to leave.</p>


